KickOS: call __atomic_*_4 for a 32-bit atomic read-modify-write on RX unless -mirq-atomics asks for
the inline form.

Against GCC 16.2.0 with gnurx-gcc-16.2.0.patch, kickos-rx-multilib.patch and
kickos-rx-dfpu-compare.patch applied, with -p1 in the GCC tree, for the rx-elf family alone. The RX
backend expands a 32-bit fetch-and-op or op-and-fetch as mvfc psw, clrpsw i, the load, the
operation and the store, then mvtc psw. In user mode the CPU ignores both writes to PSW.I without a
trap, so that sequence is a plain read-modify-write a timer interrupt can split. The patch adds
-mirq-atomics, off by default, and expands those five patterns only under it. Without it GCC calls
__atomic_fetch_<op>_4, or __sync_fetch_and_<op>_4 for a __sync builtin, as it already does for the
8- and 16-bit forms. An exchange stays an inline xchg, and a load or store a plain mov.
libstdc++'s configure then finds a call in its _Atomic_word probe.
This modifies the vendored compiler, so it carries GCC's licence, not KickOS's.

--- a/gcc/config/rx/rx.md
+++ b/gcc/config/rx/rx.md
@@ -3735,6 +3735,9 @@
    (set_attr "timings" "22")]
 )
 
+;; KickOS: interrupt masking is ignored in user mode, so each read-modify-write
+;; below is atomic in supervisor mode alone, and is expanded only under
+;; -mirq-atomics.  Without it, GCC calls __atomic_fetch_<op>_4.
 ;; read - modify - write - return old value
 (define_expand "atomic_fetch_<fetchop_name>si"
   [(set (match_operand:SI 0 "register_operand")
@@ -3742,7 +3745,7 @@
    (set (match_dup 1)
 	(FETCHOP:SI (match_dup 1) (match_operand:SI 2 "rx_source_operand")))
    (match_operand:SI 3 "const_int_operand")]		;; memory model
-  ""
+  "TARGET_IRQ_ATOMICS"
 {
   {
     rx_atomic_sequence seq (current_function_decl);
@@ -3764,7 +3767,7 @@
 	(not:SI (and:SI (match_dup 1)
 			(match_operand:SI 2 "rx_source_operand"))))
    (match_operand:SI 3 "const_int_operand")]		;; memory model
-  ""
+  "TARGET_IRQ_ATOMICS"
 {
   {
     rx_atomic_sequence seq (current_function_decl);
@@ -3790,7 +3793,7 @@
    (set (match_dup 1)
 	(FETCHOP_NO_MINUS:SI (match_dup 1) (match_dup 2)))
    (match_operand:SI 3 "const_int_operand")]		;; memory model
-  ""
+  "TARGET_IRQ_ATOMICS"
 {
   {
     rx_atomic_sequence seq (current_function_decl);
@@ -3809,7 +3812,7 @@
    (set (match_dup 1)
 	(minus:SI (match_dup 1) (match_dup 2)))
    (match_operand:SI 3 "const_int_operand")]		;; memory model
-  ""
+  "TARGET_IRQ_ATOMICS"
 {
   {
     rx_atomic_sequence seq (current_function_decl);
@@ -3828,7 +3831,7 @@
    (set (match_dup 1)
 	(not:SI (and:SI (match_dup 1) (match_dup 2))))
    (match_operand:SI 3 "const_int_operand")]		;; memory model
-  ""
+  "TARGET_IRQ_ATOMICS"
 {
   {
     rx_atomic_sequence seq (current_function_decl);
--- a/gcc/config/rx/rx.opt
+++ b/gcc/config/rx/rx.opt
@@ -244,3 +244,9 @@
 mprotect-zone
 Target Mask(PROTECT_ZONE)
 Enables the use of Renesas PROTECT_ZONE.
+
+;---------------------------------------------------
+
+mirq-atomics
+Target Mask(IRQ_ATOMICS)
+Expand a 32-bit atomic read-modify-write inline with interrupts masked, which is atomic in supervisor mode only.
